Package: kalinka-kiosk
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Depends: python3, libdrm2, libgbm1, libegl1, libegl-mesa0, libgles2, libgl1-mesa-dri, libvulkan1, libinput10, libxkbcommon0, libudev1, libsystemd0, libatomic1, libglib2.0-0t64 | libglib2.0-0, libgstreamer1.0-0, libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-0
Enhances: kalinka-server
Maintainer: Dmitry Savin <envelsavinds@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://kalinkaplayer.com
Description: Kalinka now-playing display for the server's own screen
 Shows what the Kalinka server is playing on a screen attached to it — the
 cover, the track and a progress bar, with touch controls — drawn straight to
 the display through flutter-pi, with no desktop, X or Wayland.
 .
 Turn it on in the app: Settings › EXPERT › Now-playing display on this
 machine. It starts at boot while the setting is on and restarts if it
 stops. Needs the KMS graphics
 driver (dtoverlay=vc4-kms-v3d, the default on Raspberry Pi OS) and a system
 that boots to the console.
